      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 194"
      ],
      "comment": "<span lang=\"la\">Supplicium</span> alone is often the death penalty; <span lang=\"la\">caput</span>, the head, is one’s life and civil standing, so a capital charge is <span lang=\"la\">rēs capitālis</span> and to condemn to death is <span lang=\"la\">capitis damnāre</span>, with the genitive. Every word is classical; we have found no classical instance of the phrase <span lang=\"la\">supplicium capitis</span>."
    },
